==French==

===Etymology===
Originally {{m|fr|l'||an apocopic form of ''la'', ''la'' before a vowel}} and {{m|fr|endemain}}, from {{m|fr|en}} and {{m|fr|demain}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Fr-lendemain.ogg|audio|lang=fr}}
* {{IPA|/lɑ̃dmɛ̃/|lang=fr}}

===Noun===
{{fr-noun|m}}

# the [[day]] [[after]], the [[next]] [[day]], the [[morrow]].{{jump|day after|a}}
#: ''J'ai un examen le '''lendemain''' de mon mariage''
#:: ''I have an exam the '''day after''' my wedding''

====Antonyms====
* {{jump|a|day after}} [[veille]]

